{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"fec9c247-e5b1-4e17-88d2-3a5733c1f7ae\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements about sovereignty: 1. India is free from external control. 2. Sovereignty allows every authority to ignore the Constitution. 3. The Constitution encourages respect for international law. Which are correct?\",\"hi\":\"प्रभुसत्ता के बारे में निम्न कथनों पर विचार कीजिए: 1. भारत बाहरी नियंत्रण से मुक्त है। 2. प्रभुसत्ता प्रत्येक प्राधिकारी को संविधान की उपेक्षा की अनुमति देती है। 3. संविधान अंतरराष्ट्रीय विधि के सम्मान को प्रोत्साहित करता है। कौन-से कथन सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 3\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, sections 5.4-5.5; sovereignty discussion on printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 13 and 51(c)\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fdb6a549-c2ac-49a3-88da-672f36b14229\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 51’s call to respect international law and treaty obligations is best understood as:\",\"hi\":\"अंतरराष्ट्रीय विधि और संधि-बाध्यताओं के सम्मान के लिए अनुच्छेद 51 का आह्वान सबसे उपयुक्त रूप में कैसे समझा जाना चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A transfer of all sovereignty to foreign institutions\",\"hi\":\"सारी प्रभुसत्ता विदेशी संस्थाओं को हस्तांतरित करना\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A prohibition on independent foreign policy\",\"hi\":\"स्वतंत्र विदेश नीति पर रोक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A constitutional commitment compatible with India’s voluntary exercise of sovereignty\",\"hi\":\"भारत द्वारा प्रभुसत्ता के स्वैच्छिक प्रयोग के अनुकूल संवैधानिक प्रतिबद्धता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A power of foreign courts to amend the Indian Constitution\",\"hi\":\"विदेशी न्यायालयों की भारतीय संविधान संशोधित करने की शक्ति\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, sections 5.4-5.5; sovereignty discussion on printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 51(c) and 253; NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fd526ef8-5420-4187-9745-33379543dde4\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements: 1. The Preamble mentions social, economic and political justice. 2. Article 38(1) repeats these dimensions. 3. Article 37 makes every Directive Principle directly enforceable by a court. Which are correct?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए: 1. उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) सामाजिक, आर्थिक और राजनीतिक न्याय का उल्लेख करती है। 2. अनुच्छेद 38(1) न्याय के इन्हीं आयामों को दोहराता है। 3. अनुच्छेद 37 प्रत्येक राज्य की नीति के निदेशक तत्व को न्यायालय द्वारा प्रत्यक्षतः प्रवर्तनीय बनाता है। उपर्युक्त में से कौन-से कथन सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"1 and 2 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 2\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 14-21, 25, 37-39A, 42, 46 and 51A, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; learner-facing meanings of Justice, Liberty, Equality and Fraternity\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-240; individual freedom, social justice, equality, fraternity and common national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Preamble and Articles 37-38, PDF pp. 31 and 51\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fca77839-08a8-4ca4-a2c8-68fb0c044878\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Article places elections to the Lok Sabha and State Legislative Assemblies on the basis of adult suffrage?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा अनुच्छेद लोकसभा तथा राज्य विधानसभाओं के निर्वाचनों को वयस्क मताधिकार के आधार पर संचालित करने का प्रावधान करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Article 326\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 326\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Article 324\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 324\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Article 325\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 325\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 329\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 329\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 326, PDF p. 217\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fa9ada8a-8f7d-40fd-9e5f-5cfac731cf60\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which constitutional provisions most directly operationalise the secular ethos expressed by the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) द्वारा व्यक्त पंथनिरपेक्ष भाव को कौन-से संवैधानिक प्रावधान सबसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से क्रियान्वित करते हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Articles 52-62 alone, dealing with the President\",\"hi\":\"केवल अनुच्छेद 52-62, जो राष्ट्रपति से संबंधित हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Articles 14-16 on equality and non-discrimination, read with Articles 25-28 on religious freedom\",\"hi\":\"समता और भेदभाव-निषेध संबंधी अनुच्छेद 14-16 तथा धार्मिक स्वतंत्रता संबंधी अनुच्छेद 25-28\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Articles 123 and 213 on ordinances alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल अध्यादेशों से संबंधित अनुच्छेद 123 और 213\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The provisions on inter-State trade alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल अंतरराज्यीय व्यापार संबंधी प्रावधान\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Dr Balram Singh, para 3; Evidence locator: Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Balram paragraph 3, PDF pages 2-3; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf | Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 893\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Articles 14-16 and 25-28; Balram paragraph 3, PDF pages 2-3\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f878f0d9-962f-40f4-b642-42982da329fa\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which inference about 'Democratic' in the Preamble follows from Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu?\",\"hi\":\"किहोटो होलोहन बनाम ज़ाचिल्हू से उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) के 'लोकतंत्रात्मक' शब्द के संबंध में कौन-सा निष्कर्ष निकलता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Election disputes should be decided by the political majority alone\",\"hi\":\"चुनावी विवादों का अंतिम निर्णय केवल राजनीतिक बहुमत करे\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Free and fair elections are optional conventions\",\"hi\":\"स्वतंत्र और निष्पक्ष चुनाव वैकल्पिक परंपराएँ हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Democracy is part of the basic structure, and free and fair elections with independent dispute resolution are essential democratic features\",\"hi\":\"लोकतंत्र मूल संरचना का भाग है और स्वतंत्र विवाद-निपटान सहित स्वतंत्र एवं निष्पक्ष चुनाव आवश्यक लोकतांत्रिक विशेषताएँ हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Judicial review is incompatible with parliamentary democracy\",\"hi\":\"न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन संसदीय लोकतंत्र से असंगत है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Kihoto Hollohan, headnote 8.1 and majority discussion, PDF pp. 15-16, 83; Evidence locator: headnote 8.1, PDF pages 15-16; majority discussion, PDF page 83; Direct clickable source(s): Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu: https://api.sci.gov.in/judgment/judis/12491.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/judgment/judis/12491.pdf\",\"citation\":\"1992 Supp (2) SCC 651\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"headnote 8.1, PDF pages 15-16; majority discussion, PDF page 83\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f7c564cf-7e19-4c49-91be-05842831f47b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which two dimensions are ordinarily used to explain sovereignty?\",\"hi\":\"प्रभुसत्ता को समझाने के लिए सामान्यतः किन दो आयामों का प्रयोग किया जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Judicial and legislative\",\"hi\":\"न्यायिक और विधायी\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Federal and unitary\",\"hi\":\"संघीय और एकात्मक\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Internal and external\",\"hi\":\"आंतरिक और बाह्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Civil and criminal\",\"hi\":\"सिविल और आपराधिक\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, sections 5.4-5.5; sovereignty discussion on printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, p. 49; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Preamble and Articles 13 and 245\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f675ed9a-6cc0-4500-8a20-bc3b1980747a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Does Parliament's amending power under Article 368 extend to the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"क्या अनुच्छेद 368 के अधीन संसद की संशोधन शक्ति उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) तक विस्तृत है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No, because the Preamble is outside the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"नहीं, क्योंकि उद्देशिका संविधान से बाहर है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only after a national referendum\",\"hi\":\"केवल राष्ट्रीय जनमत-संग्रह के बाद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only with unanimous approval of all States\",\"hi\":\"केवल सभी राज्यों की सर्वसम्मत स्वीकृति से\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Yes, subject to the limitations governing constitutional amendments\",\"hi\":\"हाँ, संवैधानिक संशोधनों पर लागू सीमाओं के अधीन\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"Dr Balram Singh para 2\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 835\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"para 2, judgment printed p.2 / PDF p.2\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5a8969b-a382-4a8b-bb49-accfd84ecbeb\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 25(1), freedom of conscience and religion is expressly subject to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 25(1) के अधीन अंतःकरण और धर्म की स्वतंत्रता स्पष्ट रूप से किनके अधीन है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the wishes of a local official\",\"hi\":\"केवल स्थानीय अधिकारी की इच्छा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Public order, morality, health and the other provisions of Part III\",\"hi\":\"लोक व्यवस्था, सदाचार, स्वास्थ्य और भाग III के अन्य प्रावधान\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A compulsory State religion\",\"hi\":\"अनिवार्य राज्य-धर्म\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Approval by every religious denomination\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक धार्मिक संप्रदाय की स्वीकृति\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"tit