s used in the Preamble to describe the constitutional character of India?\",\"hi\":\"भारत के संवैधानिक स्वरूप का वर्णन करने के लिए उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में प्रयुक्त पाँच अभिव्यक्तियों का सही समूह कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न, समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, लोकतंत्रात्मक, गणराज्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Federal, Socialist, Secular, Parliamentary, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संघीय, समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, संसदीय, गणराज्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Sovereign, Liberal, Secular, Presidential, Republic\",\"hi\":\"संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न, उदारवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, अध्यक्षात्मक, गणराज्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Unitary, Socialist, Religious, Democratic, Monarchy\",\"hi\":\"एकात्मक, समाजवादी, धार्मिक, लोकतंत्रात्मक, राजतंत्र\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Preamble, printed p. 31; Evidence locator: Preamble, printed page 31; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Preamble, printed page 31\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ecc88056-5610-421e-9cba-c780affb886a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"In the expression “Democratic Republic”, what does “Republic” primarily signify?\",\"hi\":\"“लोकतांत्रिक गणराज्य” पदबंध में “गणराज्य” शब्द मुख्यतः किस संवैधानिक विशेषता को व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The head of State is not a hereditary ruler\",\"hi\":\"राज्याध्यक्ष वंशानुगत शासक नहीं होता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every public employee is directly elected\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक लोक कर्मचारी प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचित होता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The legislature can never be dissolved\",\"hi\":\"विधानमंडल कभी विघटित नहीं हो सकता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The judiciary is chosen by universal voting\",\"hi\":\"न्यायपालिका सार्वभौम मतदान से चुनी जाती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, section 5.5, Democratic Republic, printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, printed p. 49; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 52 and 54\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ebf79762-eb3d-42a8-b8f5-310f3558a9b7\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement correctly distinguishes the Preamble from Fundamental Rights?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) और मौलिक अधिकारों के बीच सही अंतर कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble overrides clear Article wording whenever a broad constitutional value points in another direction\",\"hi\":\"जब कोई व्यापक संवैधानिक मूल्य दूसरी दिशा इंगित करे, तब उद्देशिका स्पष्ट अनुच्छेद-भाषा को अधिलिखित कर देती है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble and every Fundamental Right are independently enforceable in exactly the same manner\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका और प्रत्येक मौलिक अधिकार बिल्कुल समान रूप से स्वतंत्रतः प्रवर्तनीय हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Fundamental Rights merely restate political aspirations and have no operative legal effect\",\"hi\":\"मौलिक अधिकार केवल राजनीतिक आकांक्षाओं को दोहराते हैं और उनका कोई क्रियात्मक विधिक प्रभाव नहीं है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble states foundational goals, while enforceable Fundamental Rights are contained in operative constitutional provisions\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका आधारभूत लक्ष्य व्यक्त करती है, जबकि प्रवर्तनीय मौलिक अधिकार संविधान के क्रियात्मक प्रावधानों में निहित हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"Constitution Articles 13, 32 and 226; Kesavananda Bharati para 1526\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (diglot, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Kesavananda Bharati Sripadagalvaru v. State of Kerala\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29981.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(1973) 4 SCC 225\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Articles 13 printed p.36, 32 printed p.49, 226 printed p.134; Kesavananda para 1526, PDF p.345\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ea83c300-2780-4eb8-bb41-d74fc09e0ac9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which group is excluded from the Presidential electoral college described in Article 54?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 54 में निर्धारित राष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचक मंडल में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा समूह सम्मिलित नहीं है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of the Lok Sabha\",\"hi\":\"लोकसभा के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Nominated members of Parliament\",\"hi\":\"संसद के मनोनीत सदस्य\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of State Legislative Assemblies\",\"hi\":\"राज्य विधानसभाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Elected members of the Rajya Sabha\",\"hi\":\"राज्यसभा के निर्वाचित सदस्य\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, section 5.5, Democratic Republic, printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 54, PDF p. 56; NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e86ec2a7-efad-4216-91be-2bf56f4df879\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Does Indian constitutional socialism prohibit private entrepreneurship merely because it is private?\",\"hi\":\"क्या भारतीय संवैधानिक समाजवाद निजी उद्यमिता को केवल उसके निजी होने के कारण प्रतिबंधित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No; the Supreme Court has stated that socialism does not restrict private entrepreneurship and Article 19(1)(g)\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने कहा है कि समाजवाद निजी उद्यमिता और अनुच्छेद 19(1)(g) को प्रतिबंधित नहीं करता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Yes; every enterprise must be State-owned\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; प्रत्येक उद्यम राज्य के स्वामित्व में होना चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Yes; Article 19(1)(g) has no constitutional existence\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; अनुच्छेद 19(1)(g) का कोई संवैधानिक अस्तित्व नहीं है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Yes; mixed economic arrangements are unconstitutional\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; मिश्रित आर्थिक व्यवस्थाएँ असंवैधानिक हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"},{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another, 2024 INSC 893\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Order dated 25 November 2024; paragraphs 2-7, as applicable\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India, paragraphs 5-6, pp. 4-6; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 19(1)(g)\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e761f62c-8621-42b1-bb69-272fcb958ac1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements:\\n1. The Preamble may be amended under Article 368.\\n2. Any such amendment is immune from basic-structure review.\\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:\\n1. अनुच्छेद 368 के अधीन उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में संशोधन किया जा सकता है।\\n2. ऐसा कोई भी संशोधन मूल संरचना की समीक्षा से मुक्त होता है।\\nउपर्युक्त में से कौन-सा/से कथन सही है/हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"2 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Both 1 and 2\",\"hi\":\"1 और 2 दोनों\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Neither 1 nor 2\",\"hi\":\"न तो 1, न ही 2\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"Dr Balram Singh para 2\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 835\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"para 2, printed/PDF p.2\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e7083001-dfd0-406b-8b34-6af8ac31e765\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"In Puttaswamy, how did the values expressed in the Preamble assist the interpretation of Article 21?\",\"hi\":\"पुट्टस्वामी निर्णय में उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में व्यक्त मूल्यों ने अनुच्छेद 21 की व्याख्या में किस प्रकार सहायता की?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"They independently created a right to privacy outside Part III\",\"hi\":\"उन्होंने भाग III से बाहर स्वतंत्र रूप से निजता का अधिकार बनाया\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"They authorised the Court to disregard the text of Article 21\",\"hi\":\"उन्होंने न्यायालय को अनुच्छेद 21 के पाठ की उपेक्षा करने की अनुमति दी\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble's commitment to liberty and individual dignity informed an expansive reading of Article 21, while enforceability remained grounded in Part III\",\"hi\":\"स्वतंत्रता और व्यक्ति की गरिमा के प्रति उद्देशिका की प्रतिबद्धता ने अनुच्छेद 21 की व्यापक व्याख्या को दिशा दी, जबकि प्रवर्तनीयता का आधार भाग III में रहा\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"They confined Article 21 to protection against physical execution alone\",\"hi\":\"उन्होंने अनुच्छेद 21 को केवल शारीरिक रूप से जीवन समाप्त किए जाने से संरक्षण तक सीमित कर दिया\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"Puttaswamy paras 95-96 and 113\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(2017) 10 SCC 1\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"paras 95-96, PDF pp.92-93; para 113, PDF pp.108-109\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e57fc727-48d0-4702-8972-55e5404ee4ec\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why is the statement “India ceases to be a republic because citizens do not directly elect the President” incorrect?\",\"hi\":\"यह कथन क्यों गलत है कि “नागरिक राष्ट्रपति का प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन नहीं करते, इसलिए भारत गणराज्य नहीं है”?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A republic requires a non-hereditary head; the Constitution validly provides indirect election\",\"hi\":\"गणराज्य में गैर-वंशानुगत राज्याध्यक्ष आवश्यक है; संविधान वैध रूप से अप्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन देता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The President inherits office automatically\",\"hi\":\"राष्ट्रपति स्वतः पद विरासत में पाता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"India has no constitutional head\",\"hi\":\"भारत का कोई संवैधानिक राज्याध्यक्ष नहीं है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 54 requires direct voting by every citizen\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 54 प्रत्येक नागरिक का प्रत्यक्ष मतदान आवश्यक करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, section 5.5, Democratic Republic, printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, printed p. 49; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 54\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e495b278-1e9c-41e6-ba4b-e6e099043671\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which combination best reflects the essential features of democratic government?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा संयोजन लोकतांत्रिक सरकार की अनिवार्य विशेषताओं को सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त रूप से व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary, secret and permanent\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत, गुप्त और स्थायी\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Elected, responsible and accountable to the people\",\"hi\":\"निर्वाचित, उत्तरदायी और जनता के प्रति जवाबदेह\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Military, unreviewable and unelected\",\"hi\":\"सैन्य, पुनरावलोकन से परे और अनिर्वाचित\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Nominated, hereditary and unaccountable\",\"hi\":\"मनोनीत, वंशानुगत और गैर-जवाबदेह\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 52, 54-58, 61-62, 75(3), 79, 81, 83, 324-326, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Democratic and Republic on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; popular participation, universal franchise and constitutional philosophy\"},{\"title\":\"Senior Secondary Political Science (317), Lesson 5: Preamble and Salient Features\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS)\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Lesson 5, section 5.5, Democratic Republic, printed p. 49\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"NIOS Political Science (317), Lesson 5, section 5.5, printed p. 49\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e45899c3-dd1f-4cb2-aac7-092ada8df7af\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"With reference to the Preamble, what was the view in the Berubari advisory opinion that was later disapproved in Kesavananda Bharati?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) के संदर्भ में, बेरूबारी परामर्श मत का कौन-सा दृष्टिकोण बाद में केशवानंद भारती में अस्वीकार किया गया?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"That the Preamble contains the whole Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कि उद्देशिका में पूरा संविधान समाहित है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"That the Preamble was not a part of the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कि उद्देशिका संविधान का भाग नहीं थी\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"That the Preamble could never assist interpretation\",\"hi\":\"कि उद्देशिका कभी व्याख्या में सहायता नहीं कर सकती\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"That Article 368 was absent from the Constitution\",\"hi\":\"कि संविधान में अनुच्छेद 368 नहीं था\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"Ashoka Kumar Thakur para 91; Kesavananda Bharati paras 1524-1526\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Ashoka Kumar Thakur v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/31353.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(2008) 6 SCC 1\"},{\"title\":\"Kesavananda Bharati Sripadagalvaru v. State of Kerala\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29981.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(1973) 4 SCC 225\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Ashoka para 91, PDF pp.86-87; Kesavananda paras 1524-1526, PDF p.345\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e2748744-11f2-416b-81e8-124904ac6002\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"According to the Supreme Court's Article 370 judgment, which statement best reflects the word 'Sovereign' in the Preamble?\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के अनुच्छेद 370 निर्णय के अनुसार उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) के 'संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न' शब्द को कौन-सा कथन सबसे सही रूप से व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The Constitution of India is the sovereign governing document, and constituent States do not possess a parallel independent sovereignty\",\"hi\":\"भारत का संविधान संप्रभु शासकीय दस्तावेज है और संघटक राज्य समानांतर स्वतंत्र संप्रभुता नहीं रखते\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Every State Constitution is legally equal to the Constitution of India\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक राज्य का संविधान भारत के संविधान के विधिक रूप से समान है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Sovereignty belongs exclusively to Parliament rather than the constitutional order\",\"hi\":\"संप्रभुता संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के बजाय केवल संसद में निहित है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The Preamble recognises separate international sovereignty for each State\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका प्रत्येक राज्य की पृथक अंतरराष्ट्रीय संप्रभुता मानती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: In Re: Article 370, paras 61-62, PDF p. 53; Evidence locator: paragraphs 61-62, PDF page 53; Direct clickable source(s): In Re: Article 370 of the Constitution: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/29796/29796_2019_1_1501_49019_Judgement_11-Dec-2023.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"In Re: Article 370 of the Constitution\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2019/29796/29796_2019_1_1501_49019_Judgement_11-Dec-2023.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2023 INSC 1058\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"paragraphs 61-62, PDF page 53\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e256ad19-539d-4451-ae4f-d27bbade1cd9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does 'Fraternity' in the Preamble expressly assure?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) में 'बंधुता' स्पष्ट रूप से क्या सुनिश्चित करती है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"The dignity of the individual and the unity and integrity of the Nation\",\"hi\":\"व्यक्ति की गरिमा तथा राष्ट्र की एकता और अखंडता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Equality of income in every occupation\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक व्यवसाय में आय की समता\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A hereditary right to public office\",\"hi\":\"सार्वजनिक पद का वंशानुगत अधिकार\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Unrestricted exercise of every claimed freedom\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक दावा की गई स्वतंत्रता का अप्रतिबंधित प्रयोग\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Preamble, printed p. 31; Evidence locator: Preamble, printed page 31; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Preamble, printed page 31\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"dff739f8-5cb4-45a2-bcda-0c738e19220b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does the word 'Democratic' in the Preamble most directly require from government?\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) का 'लोकतंत्रात्मक' शब्द सरकार से सबसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से क्या अपेक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Government by hereditary office-holders not answerable to citizens\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत पदाधिकारियों की ऐसी सरकार जो नागरिकों के प्रति उत्तरदायी न हो\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Government chosen through constitutional processes and responsible and accountable to the people\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक प्रक्रियाओं से चुनी गई और जनता के प्रति जिम्मेदार तथा जवाबदेह सरकार\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Government in which elections permanently remove public accountability\",\"hi\":\"ऐसी सरकार जिसमें चुनाव सार्वजनिक जवाबदेही की आवश्यकता स्थायी रूप से समाप्त कर दें\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Government controlled by unelected private organisations\",\"hi\":\"निर्वाचित न होने वाले निजी संगठनों द्वारा नियंत्रित सरकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Electoral Bonds judgment, para 201; NIOS section 5.5; Evidence locator: Supreme Court paragraph 201, PDF page 140; NIOS section 5.5, printed page 49; Direct clickable source(s): Association for Democratic Reforms v. Union of India: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/27935/27935_2017_1_1501_50573_Judgement_15-Feb-2024.pdf | Preamble and the Salient Features of the Constitution of India, Lesson 5: https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Association for Democratic Reforms v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/27935/27935_2017_1_1501_50573_Judgement_15-Feb-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"2024 INSC 113\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Preamble and the Salient Features of the Constitution of India, Lesson 5\",\"institution\":\"National Institute of Open Schooling\",\"url\":\"https://digital.nios.ac.in/content/317en/317EL5.pdf\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Supreme Court paragraph 201, PDF page 140; NIOS section 5.5, printed page 49\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"de39c0c2-80e4-42ce-9aa5-e2cb2475c7ed\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which pair best captures the justice orientation of Indian socialism identified by the Supreme Court?\",\"hi\":\"कौन-सा युग्म सर्वोच्च न्यायालय द्वारा पहचाने गए भारतीय समाजवाद के न्याय-अभिमुखीकरण को सबसे अच्छी तरह व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Military and diplomatic justice\",\"hi\":\"सैन्य और कूटनीतिक न्याय\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Procedural and punitive justice only\",\"hi\":\"केवल प्रक्रियात्मक और दंडात्मक न्याय\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Economic and social justice\",\"hi\":\"आर्थिक और सामाजिक न्याय\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary and corporate privilege\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत और निगमित विशेषाधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"},{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another, 2024 INSC 893\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":