ce_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 14-21, 25, 37-39A, 42, 46 and 51A, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; learner-facing meanings of Justice, Liberty, Equality and Fraternity\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-240; individual freedom, social justice, equality, fraternity and common national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Articles 41-43, PDF p. 52\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d8a9ce49-4d4a-44e2-9398-eabbbf075cfb\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A constitutional clause is reasonably open to two interpretations. One interpretation advances the Preamble's constitutional values and the other frustrates them, while both fit the text. What is the sounder approach?\",\"hi\":\"किसी संवैधानिक खंड की दो युक्तिसंगत व्याख्याएँ संभव हैं। एक उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) के संवैधानिक मूल्यों को आगे बढ़ाती है और दूसरी उन्हें बाधित करती है, जबकि दोनों पाठ से मेल खाती हैं। अधिक उचित दृष्टिकोण क्या होगा?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Prefer the interpretation that gives the court the widest possible discretion, regardless of the text\",\"hi\":\"पाठ की परवाह किए बिना उस व्याख्या को प्राथमिकता देना जो न्यायालय को अधिकतम विवेक दे\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Prefer the interpretation consistent with the Preamble, subject to the constitutional text\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक पाठ के अधीन उद्देशिका-संगत व्याख्या को प्राथमिकता देना\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Treat the Preamble as creating a power that the constitutional text does not confer\",\"hi\":\"उद्देशिका को ऐसी शक्ति निर्मित करने वाला मानना जो संवैधानिक पाठ प्रदान नहीं करता\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Select the interpretation least connected with the Constitution's stated objectives\",\"hi\":\"उस व्याख्या को चुनना जिसका संविधान के घोषित उद्देश्यों से सबसे कम संबंध हो\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"Kesavananda Bharati para 1526; Ashoka Kumar Thakur para 91\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Kesavananda Bharati Sripadagalvaru v. State of Kerala\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29981.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(1973) 4 SCC 225\"},{\"title\":\"Ashoka Kumar Thakur v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/31353.pdf\",\"citation\":\"(2008) 6 SCC 1\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Kesavananda para 1526, PDF p.345; Ashoka para 91, PDF pp.86-87\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d5cc40fb-8db1-4d43-9545-4fc47750120f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 39(d) directs State policy towards securing:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 39(d) राज्य की नीति को निम्नलिखित में से किस लक्ष्य की प्राप्ति की ओर निर्देशित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary public offices\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत लोक पद\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Equal pay for equal work for both men and women\",\"hi\":\"पुरुषों और महिलाओं दोनों के लिए समान कार्य का समान वेतन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A special electoral roll by sex\",\"hi\":\"लिंग के आधार पर विशेष निर्वाचक नामावली\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Abolition of all private occupations\",\"hi\":\"सभी निजी व्यवसायों का उन्मूलन\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 14-21, 25, 37-39A, 42, 46 and 51A, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; learner-facing meanings of Justice, Liberty, Equality and Fraternity\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-240; individual freedom, social justice, equality, fraternity and common national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 39(a), (d) and (f), PDF pp. 51-52\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d5b1f4a1-935f-47e4-b526-bd9a8b6d9828\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Consider the following statements: 1. India’s secular constitutional ethos existed in substantive provisions even before the word was inserted in the Preamble. 2. Secularism prevents the State from regulating every secular activity associated with religion. 3. The State may neither favour its own religion nor penalise the practice of a faith. Which are correct?\",\"hi\":\"निम्न कथनों पर विचार कीजिए: 1. उद्देशिका में शब्द जोड़े जाने से पहले भी भारत का पंथनिरपेक्ष संवैधानिक लोकाचार मूल प्रावधानों में विद्यमान था। 2. पंथनिरपेक्षता राज्य को धर्म से जुड़ी प्रत्येक लौकिक गतिविधि के विनियमन से रोकती है। 3. राज्य न अपने धर्म का पक्ष ले सकता है, न किसी आस्था के आचरण को दंडित कर सकता है। कौन-से कथन सही हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"1 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"1 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 1 और 3\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"2 and 3 only\",\"hi\":\"केवल 2 और 3\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"1, 2 and 3\",\"hi\":\"1, 2 और 3\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"},{\"title\":\"Dr Balram Singh and Others v. Union of India and Another, 2024 INSC 893\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2020/13773/13773_2020_1_39_57487_Judgement_25-Nov-2024.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Order dated 25 November 2024; paragraphs 2-7, as applicable\"},{\"title\":\"Ashwini Kumar Upadhyay v. Union of India and Others\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/6310/6310_2023_3_23_42310_Judgement_27-Feb-2023.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Judgment dated 27 February 2023; paragraphs 5-10, as applicable\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Dr Balram Singh v. Union of India, paragraphs 3-4, pp. 2-4; Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 25(2); Ashwini Kumar Upadhyay v. Union of India, paragraphs 5 and 7\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d408b378-a526-4c63-b1fe-0cde472ad1e0\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Does the word 'Republic' in the Preamble require the President of India to be directly elected by all citizens?\",\"hi\":\"क्या उद्देशिका (प्रस्तावना) का 'गणराज्य' शब्द भारत के राष्ट्रपति का सभी नागरिकों द्वारा प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन अनिवार्य करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No; a republic requires a non-hereditary constitutional head, and Article 54 provides indirect election through an electoral college\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; गणराज्य गैर-वंशानुगत संवैधानिक राज्याध्यक्ष की अपेक्षा करता है और अनुच्छेद 54 निर्वाचक मंडल द्वारा अप्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन की व्यवस्था करता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Yes; every republic must elect its head by direct popular vote\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; प्रत्येक गणराज्य को राज्याध्यक्ष का प्रत्यक्ष जनमत से निर्वाचन करना चाहिए\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Yes; indirect election converts the system into a monarchy\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; अप्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन व्यवस्था को राजतंत्र बना देता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No; because the President is appointed for life by Parliament\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; क्योंकि राष्ट्रपति को संसद आजीवन नियुक्त करती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: Constitution, Article 54, printed p. 56; Evidence locator: Article 54, printed page 56; Direct clickable source(s): The Constitution of India, diglot edition: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf; Confidence: high; Originality: independently written; no PYQ, textbook exercise, coaching question, or copyrighted explanation has been copied.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India, diglot edition\",\"institution\":\"Government of India, Legislative Department\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Article 54, printed page 56\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d2a43b3a-5088-41d8-9bea-c5604c718a9b\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 28(3), a person in a State-recognised or State-aided educational institution cannot be required to attend religious instruction or worship without:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 28(3) के अधीन राज्य-मान्यताप्राप्त या राज्य-सहायता प्राप्त शैक्षणिक संस्था में किसी व्यक्ति को किसके बिना धार्मिक शिक्षा या उपासना में भाग लेने को बाध्य नहीं किया जा सकता?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"His consent, or the guardian’s consent if he is a minor\",\"hi\":\"उसकी सहमति, या अवयस्क होने पर उसके संरक्षक की सहमति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A resolution of Parliament\",\"hi\":\"संसद का संकल्प\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"A foreign treaty\",\"hi\":\"विदेशी संधि\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A special electoral roll\",\"hi\":\"विशेष निर्वाचक नामावली\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-16: Constitution of India; NCERT Class IX and XI; NIOS and Supreme Court official documents where applicable.\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Preamble; Articles 13-16, 19(1)(g), 25-30, 38-43, 47, 51, 51A(e), 253 and 325, as applicable to the question\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Democratic Politics-I, Class IX, Chapter 2: Constitutional Design (Reprint 2025-26)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/iess402.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 28-30; meanings of Sovereign, Socialist and Secular on printed p. 29\"},{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 10: The Philosophy of the Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps210.pdf\",\"citation\":\"Printed pp. 225-239; constitutional philosophy, individual freedom, social justice, secularism and national identity\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Legislative Department, Constitution of India, 2026 Hindi-English edition, Article 28(3), PDF p. 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d2938359-b185-4f63-960b-c84455b251ba\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which statement best captures the fundamental meaning of justice?\",\"hi\":\"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन न्याय की मूल अवधारणा को सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त रूप से व्यक्त करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"